                "role": "assistant",
                "content": "To create a board where the largest monochromatic square has a side length of $\\frac{N-1}{2}=10$, we need to ensure that there are no squares with a side length of $11$ or more.\n\nWe can start by creating a $10\\times10$ blue square in the top-left corner. This square will be monochromatic and have a side length of $10$.\n\nNext, we can create $10$ red columns, each with $10$ cells, to the right of the blue square. These columns will ensure that there are no red squares with a side length of $11$ or more.\n\nWe can then create $10$ blue rows, each with $10$ cells, below the blue square. These rows will ensure that there are no blue squares with a side length of $11$ or more.\n\nNow, we can fill in the remaining cells with a checkerboard pattern of blue and red. This will ensure that there are no monochromatic squares with a side length of $11$ or more.\n\nHere is the completed board:\n\n$\\boxed{\\begin{array}{cccccccccccccccccccccccc}\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nb & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & r & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b & b \\\\\nr & r & r &